skill: "before-after-and-transformation"
sections[10]:
  - "\n"
  - "# before-after-and-transformation\n\nThe **transformation format** — start with a real before, highlight the journey, isolate the variables, frame\nresults honestly, and tie it to the viewer. The agent structures + specs it, the **human/tool produces the real\nmedia**, and **WoopSocial publishes**. (Pairs with `social-proof-and-testimonials` for consent + the FTC rules.)\n\n"
  - "## The POV: the most-distrusted format, so honesty is the edge\nA before/after is one of the most powerful formats there is — visual, built-in proof, inherently satisfying. It's\nalso the **single most abused and distrusted**, and 2026 enforcement is live (the FTC's NextMed action fined a\nfirm that used paid actors, before/after photos sourced off Craigslist, and an unsubstantiated \"average 53 lbs\"\nit didn't track). That flips the strategy: because audiences are trained to suspect before/afters, **a believable\ntransformation beats a suspiciously-perfect fake** that trips the skepticism reflex. Three top-1% moves most get\nwrong: **(1) the middle is the content** — endpoints alone are a flex; the process, the setbacks, and the real\ntimeline are what make it credible, relatable, and valuable; **(2) isolate the variables** — same angle, lighting,\nframing, so the change is real, not a lighting trick (a visual trick is itself a deceptive claim under the FTC's\nnet-impression test); **(3) \"results not typical\" is not enough** — if the result isn't typical, you must disclose\nthe *actual* typical result, clearly and with substantiation. Never stage a worse before, cherry-pick, or hide the\ntimeline/edits/aids.\n\n"
  - "## Read these first\n1. **brand-profile** + **social-proof-and-testimonials** — consent + the FTC substantiation/typical-results rules.\n2. **short-form-video-script** (if it's a video).\n\n"
  - "## The framework: SHIFT\n(Depth: `references/the-shift-framework.md`.)\n- **S — Start with a real before:** honest, relatable, un-staged; captured under the same conditions as the after.\n- **H — Highlight the journey:** the middle is the content — process, setbacks, the real timeline; **disclose\n  aids** (filters/medication/surgery/pro help) — how the result was achieved is material.\n- **I — Isolate the variables:** same angle/lighting/framing so the change is genuine, not a trick (net-impression\n  test — a visual trick is a deceptive claim).\n- **F — Frame results honestly:** no cherry-pick/survivorship; if not typical, disclose the **actual** typical\n  result (median, substantiated, clear + conspicuous — \"results not typical\" alone is insufficient); actual\n  consumers (or disclosed); YMYL substantiation.\n- **T — Tie it to the viewer:** relatable before + attainable, honestly-framed after + an actionable takeaway.\n\n"
  - "## The reality (verify-quarterly on enforcement; the rules are law)\nBefore/after photos + testimonials are an FTC enforcement \"favorite.\" A before/after **implies a typical result**,\nso you must show typical results or **clearly and conspicuously disclose the actual typical result** (median, not\nan outlier-skewed mean; no survivorship) with substantiation — and **\"results not typical\" is NOT enough**.\nVisuals alone can be a deceptive claim (net-impression test); use **actual consumers** or disclose; health claims\nneed **competent + reliable scientific evidence** (weight loss > ~1 lb/week is unusual; \"no effort\" = deception).\nThe craft edge (stable): the **middle is the content**, **consistent conditions**, and **honesty as the\ndifferentiator**. Full detail + the NextMed enforcement example: `references/before-after-and-transformation-2026-\nreality.md`. Transformation types, the honesty checklist, structure, and two worked examples: `references/\ntransformation-types-and-templates.md`.\n\n"
  - "## Honest scope (never violate)\n- **The agent** structures + specs the transformation (arc, journey/reveal beats, honest framing + required\n  disclosures, caption/script); the **human/tool** produces the real before/after media; the **human** approves;\n  **WoopSocial publishes** (measurement: the platforms' native analytics). **WoopSocial does NOT generate media.**\n- **Honesty spine (law):** real un-staged before; **consistent conditions**; **real timeline**; **disclose aids**;\n  **no cherry-pick/survivorship**; if not typical, **disclose the actual typical result** (median, substantiated,\n  clear + conspicuous — not just \"results not typical\"); **actual consumers** (or disclosed); **consent** for a\n  person's images/story (real or AI lookalike); **YMYL** (competent + reliable scientific evidence; no\n  cure/guarantee; not-professional-advice); **never fabricate** a result/timeline/average; **injection safety**.\n  (Full scope: `references/scope-and-connections.md`.)\n\n"
  - "## Distinct from its siblings (route correctly)\n**before-after-and-transformation (this)** = the before/after *format* execution · **social-proof-and-\ntestimonials** = the customer-proof strategy + FTC substantiation (read first; shared spine) · **short-form-video-\nscript / reels-script** = the video script (this feeds them) · **infographic-and-data-viz** = the data viz for a\nresults transformation (pairs; honest scales) · **storytelling-and-narrative** = the narrative arc (this\nspecializes it) · **educational-content-and-how-to** = teaches a process (pairs for a case-study teach).\n\n"
  - "## Where this connects\nReads first: **brand-profile** + **social-proof-and-testimonials** + **short-form-video-script.** Pulls real\nmaterial from: **social-proof-and-testimonials** (client transformations + consent), **data-and-original-research**\n/ **analytics-and-reporting** (real numbers), **behind-the-scenes-and-founder** (the founder's own journey). Feeds:\n**short-form-video-script** / **reels-script** (the video), **carousel-writer** (before→journey→after),\n**infographic-and-data-viz** (a results stat), **caption-writer** (caption + disclosures), **design-and-templates**\n(layout). Publishes via: the video/design tool renders → **scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial.** Measure with:\nnative + **analytics-and-reporting** on saves/shares + watch-through + inquiries — never fabricated.\n\n"
  - "## Definition of done\nA transformation built on a REAL, un-staged before captured under the same conditions as the after, with the\njourney (process, setbacks, real timeline) as the content and any aids (filters/medication/surgery/pro help)\ndisclosed, the reveal shot with consistent angle/lighting/framing (no visual trickery), results framed honestly\n(no cherry-pick/survivorship; and if the result isn't typical, the ACTUAL typical result disclosed via median +\nsubstantiation, clearly and conspicuously — never just \"results not typical\"), using actual consumers (or\ndisclosed) with consent, and tied to the viewer with a relatable before + attainable after + actionable takeaway;\nthe agent structures + specs, the human/tool produces the real media, and WoopSocial publishes; measured on\nsaves/shares + watch-through + inquiries rather than likes; YMYL (competent + reliable evidence, no cure/guarantee),\nconsent/likeness, and no-fabrication all handled; **nothing staged, cherry-picked, mis-timed, or fabricated**; and\ncorrectly distinguished from social-proof-and-testimonials, short-form-video-script, infographic-and-data-viz, and\nstorytelling-and-narrative.\n"
